# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EAS Build archive scope — ALLOWLIST (studio monorepo)
#
# The whole studio shares ONE git repo, and EAS uploads from the repo root.
# THE RULE: ignore EVERYTHING, then re-include ONLY the one app being built.
# This means any NEW sibling project (or its .venv / node_modules / backups) is
# excluded automatically — you never have to add it here.
#
# To build a DIFFERENT project in future: change the single app path in section 2
# (and its inner-exclusions in section 3) to point at that project's app folder.
#
# This only controls what the cloud build UPLOADS. It never deletes local files.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 1) Ignore everything, at every level.
/*

# 2) Walk back down and re-include ONLY the app we build (currently: Let Me Check).
#    Each parent level must be re-included before its child (gitignore rule).
!/projects/
/projects/*
!/projects/let-me-check/
/projects/let-me-check/*
!/projects/let-me-check/lmc-app/

# 3) Inside that app, still skip regenerable / heavy dirs — EAS rebuilds these
#    on its servers, so they never need uploading.
/projects/let-me-check/lmc-app/ios/
/projects/let-me-check/lmc-app/android/
/projects/let-me-check/lmc-app/node_modules/
/projects/let-me-check/lmc-app/.expo/
/projects/let-me-check/lmc-app/_archive/
/projects/let-me-check/lmc-app/*.bak
